LLVMSupport: files without mmap, statvfs, link or umask; the main
executable from argv[0]

Failure: Unix/Path.inc does not compile for the kit: `GetMainExecutable is
not implemented on this host yet` (Path.inc:338: no dladdr, no /proc);
`no member named 'f_flags' in 'statvfs'`/`MNT_LOCAL` (Path.inc:559); and it
references mmap, munmap, posix_madvise (mapped_file_region), statvfs
(disk_space, is_local), link (create_hard_link) and umask (getUmask), none
of which the kit, its adapter or Picolibc defines.
Change, under LLVM_ABSD_KIT only: getMainExecutable resolves argv[0] (a
name with a slash against the working directory, else through PATH) with
the adapter's realpath; is_local answers true for anything the kit can
stat (ABSD has no remote filesystem); disk_space and create_hard_link are
refused (not_supported / function_not_supported); getUmask is 022, the
mask the kit's fixed 0644 creation mode implies; a read-only or private
mapped_file_region is the file's bytes read into a page-aligned heap block
(zero past end of file, descriptor position restored) and a shared
(readwrite) one is refused; MemoryBuffer never chooses mmap (files are read
into the heap); FileOutputBuffer always builds in memory and writes on
commit (what F_no_mmap does).
Behaviour preserved: other platforms unchanged. On ABSD every reader sees
the same bytes a mapping would show; writers see the same file after
commit; what cannot be honoured (shared mappings, hard links, disk space)
is refused, not approximated.
Upstreamability: needs an ABSD OS in LLVM; the MemoryBuffer and
FileOutputBuffer choices would be upstream as a "no mmap" platform switch
(upstream has none today; WebAssembly/WASI ports carry similar patches).

